---
import { Alert, Code, CodeTabs, CopyButton, Image, Link, Prose, Table } from '@santi020k/lumen-astro'

import ArticleReading from '../../../../../packages/lumen/templates/astro/article-reading/src/lumen/article-reading.astro'
import { getGuide } from '../../data/guides'
import BaseLayout from '../../layouts/BaseLayout.astro'

const guide = getGuide('/guides/build-an-editorial-article')

const chapters = [
  { id: 'reading', label: 'Start with the reading path' },
  { id: 'content', label: 'Connect quotations and figures' },
  { id: 'install', label: 'Install the editable recipe' },
  { id: 'examples', label: 'Keep code examples connected' },
  { id: 'tables', label: 'Give wide tables room' },
  { id: 'verify', label: 'Verify enlarged text' }
]

const commands = [
  { value: 'pnpm', label: 'pnpm', language: 'shell', code: 'pnpm add @santi020k/lumen-astro\npnpm add -D @santi020k/lumen\npnpm exec lumen add article-reading --target astro' },
  { value: 'npm', label: 'npm', language: 'shell', code: 'npm install @santi020k/lumen-astro\nnpm install -D @santi020k/lumen\nnpx lumen add article-reading --target astro' }
]

const auditCommands = [
  { value: 'pnpm', label: 'pnpm', language: 'shell', code: 'pnpm add -D @playwright/test\npnpm exec playwright install chromium\npnpm exec lumen audit-rendered http://127.0.0.1:4321/guides/build-an-editorial-article --viewport 320x844 --text-scale 200 --json' },
  { value: 'npm', label: 'npm', language: 'shell', code: 'npm install -D @playwright/test\nnpx playwright install chromium\nnpx lumen audit-rendered http://127.0.0.1:4321/guides/build-an-editorial-article --viewport 320x844 --text-scale 200 --json' }
]

const layoutSource = `---
import UIPrimitives from '@santi020k/lumen-astro/runtime'
---
<html lang="en">
  <body>
    <slot />
    <UIPrimitives />
  </body>
</html>`

const proseSource = `---
import { Image, Prose } from '@santi020k/lumen-astro'
---
<Prose appearance="editorial">
  <h2 id="principle">Keep the reading path clear</h2>
  <blockquote>
    <p>Your quoted passage.</p>
    <footer>From <cite>The quoted work</cite></footer>
  </blockquote>
  <figure>
    <Image src="/illustration.svg" alt="Describe the image" width="960" height="600" radius="none" />
    <figcaption>Your authored caption.</figcaption>
  </figure>
</Prose>`

const articleSource = `---
import ArticleReading from '../lumen/article-reading.astro'
const chapters = [{ id: 'design', label: 'Design the reading path' }]
---
<ArticleReading articleId="story" chapters={chapters}>
  <section id="design">
    <h2>Design the reading path</h2>
    <p>Your original article goes here.</p>
  </section>
</ArticleReading>`
---

<BaseLayout title={guide.title} description={guide.description} article={{ author: guide.author, publishedAt: guide.publishedAt }}>
  <main class="article-guide">
    <header class="article-guide__header">
      <Link href="/guides">All guides</Link>
      <h1>{guide.title}</h1>
      <p>Give readers a clear path through a long technical story. Try this page’s contents menu,
        switch its package-manager examples, and scroll the comparison table with your keyboard.</p>
      <p class="article-guide__context">Inspired by the reading experience on{' '}
        <Link href="https://santi020k.com">santi020k.com v5</Link>. This example uses original instructional content.</p>
      <Alert>This guide demonstrates the Lumen 5 candidate. Check registry availability before installing.
        Use the matching package versions and CLI when following the examples.</Alert>
    </header>
    <ArticleReading articleId="editorial-story" chapters={chapters}>
      <Prose appearance="editorial">
      <section id="reading">
        <h2>Start with the reading path</h2>
        <p>A reader may arrive from search halfway through an article, browse its headings on a phone,
          or enlarge the text before reading a code example. Keep the article in document order and
          let its controls adapt to the space around it.</p>
        <p>The editable <code>article-reading</code> recipe composes Lumen’s Anchor, Collapsible,
          SkipLink, and ScrollProgress. A wider screen gets a contents rail. A narrow screen gets
          a native disclosure. Reading progress measures this article, so the site footer does not
          become part of the story.</p>
        <p>On the released website, some tab, anchor, and progress behaviors were carried by a
          version-pinned consumer patch. The Lumen 5 candidate includes the shared fixes.
          Verify the upgrade against your own article before removing a patch.</p>
        <Link href="/docs/migrations/v4-to-v5">Read the v4 to v5 migration guide</Link>
      </section>
      <section id="content">
        <h2>Connect quotations and figures</h2>
        <p>The editorial appearance of <Link href="/docs/components/prose">Prose</Link> keeps paragraphs
          at a readable measure while media and technical examples use the available width. It styles
          the original headings, quotations, and captions without rewriting their content or IDs.</p>
        <blockquote>
          <p>A clear reading path should survive a change in theme, language, or viewport.</p>
          <footer>From <cite>Example editorial notes</cite> — illustrative content for this guide.</footer>
        </blockquote>
        <figure>
          <Image alt="An illustrated mountain landscape reflected in a lake" height="600" radius="none" src="/comparison-before.svg" width="960" />
          <figcaption>An illustrative figure keeps its caption and image together as the reading column narrows.</figcaption>
        </figure>
        <p>Keep the quoted source in a native <code>cite</code> element. Write a useful image alternative
          independently of the visible caption, and keep <code>figcaption</code> inside the same
          <code>figure</code>. Lumen components such as Code and charts retain their own figure styling.</p>
        <Code appearance="editorial" code={proseSource} copy copyLabel="Copy code" label="Semantic editorial content" language="astro" variant="block" scrollCue />
      </section>
      <section id="install">
        <h2>Install the editable recipe</h2>
        <p>Add the Astro adapter and CLI, then copy the recipe into your application. The CLI owns
          installation and diagnostics. The copied composition belongs to your app, while its imports
          continue to receive package-owned primitive fixes.</p>
        <CodeTabs ariaLabel="Install the article recipe" items={commands} storageKey="editorial-guide-manager" wrap={false} scrollCue />
        <p>Mount the runtime once in your root layout. Astro components include their selective CSS.</p>
        <Code variant="block" copy wrap code={layoutSource} language="astro" label="Root layout" />
        <p>Give each heading a stable, unique ID and pass the same IDs into the recipe.</p>
        <Code variant="block" copy wrap code={articleSource} language="astro" label="Article page" />
        <Link href="/docs/components/anchor">Explore the Anchor contract</Link>
      </section>
      <section id="examples">
        <h2>Keep code examples connected</h2>
        <p>Both package-manager examples on this page share one <code>storageKey</code>. Choose npm
          above and the verification commands below follow that choice. The group you activate keeps
          focus while the other updates in place. The complete source remains available for copying.</p>
        <p>Use a shared key only for examples representing the same choice. Keep an unrelated language
          picker independent. Long lines scroll within their own named region, with a cue when more
          content lies outside it.</p>
        <Link href="/docs/components/code-tabs">Explore CodeTabs</Link>
      </section>
      <section id="tables">
        <h2>Give wide tables room</h2>
        <p>This table preserves its caption and headers. Focus the scroll region and use the arrow
          keys at narrow widths. The surrounding article continues to fit the viewport.</p>
        <Table scrollCue stickyFirstColumn aria-label="Compare the responsibilities in an editorial page">
          <table>
            <caption>Responsibilities in this article</caption>
            <thead><tr><th scope="col">Layer</th><th scope="col">Maintains</th><th scope="col">Example</th></tr></thead>
            <tbody>
              <tr><th scope="row">Lumen primitive</th><td>Keyboard behavior and semantic controls</td><td>Anchor, CodeTabs, ScrollProgress</td></tr>
              <tr><th scope="row">Editable recipe</th><td>Responsive composition and local labels</td><td>Contents rail and mobile disclosure</td></tr>
              <tr><th scope="row">Application</th><td>Writing, routing, localization, and content policy</td><td>Heading IDs and publishing decisions</td></tr>
            </tbody>
          </table>
        </Table>
        <p>For Markdown-generated tables, apply the same contract during rendering.</p>
        <Link href="/guides/readable-markdown-tables">Build the Markdown table integration</Link>
      </section>
      <section id="verify">
        <h2>Verify enlarged text</h2>
        <p>Run a built preview locally and audit this route at 320px with 200% text. The opt-in text
          scale check reports clipped control text alongside document overflow. Review each finding
          in the rendered page, including controls inside disclosures and overlays after opening them.</p>
        <CodeTabs ariaLabel="Audit the article with enlarged text" items={auditCommands} storageKey="editorial-guide-manager" wrap={false} scrollCue />
        <p>Repeat at desktop width and in both themes. Follow a contents link, switch package managers,
          copy a complete example, and navigate away and back. Disable JavaScript to verify that
          headings, the mobile disclosure, and source examples remain readable. Use keyboard and
          screen-reader checks to verify the reading order and focus destination.</p>
        <Link href="/docs/components/scroll-progress">Explore scoped reading progress</Link>
        <div class="article-guide__share">
          <CopyButton value="https://lumen.santi020k.com/guides/build-an-editorial-article/" label="Copy guide link">Copy guide link</CopyButton>
          <Link href="/templates/editorial">Explore the editorial recipes</Link>
        </div>
      </section>
      </Prose>
    </ArticleReading>
  </main>
</BaseLayout>

<style>
  .article-guide { max-inline-size: 80rem; margin-inline: auto; padding: clamp(1rem, 4vw, 3rem); overflow-wrap: anywhere; }
  .article-guide__header { max-inline-size: 52rem; margin-block-end: 3rem; }
  h1 { margin-block: 1rem; font-size: clamp(2rem, 5vw, 3.75rem); line-height: 1.12; letter-spacing: -0.035em; color: hsl(var(--ink)); }
  .article-guide__header p { margin-block: 1rem; line-height: 1.8; color: hsl(var(--ink-soft)); }
  section { min-inline-size: 0; scroll-margin-block-start: 8rem; }
  section + section { margin-block-start: 3rem; }
  .article-guide__context { color: hsl(var(--ink-muted)); }
  .article-guide__share { display: flex; flex-wrap: wrap; gap: 1.25rem; align-items: center; margin-block-start: 2rem; }
  .article-guide__share :global(button) { max-inline-size: 100%; white-space: normal; overflow-wrap: anywhere; }
  table { min-inline-size: 34rem; }
  caption { text-align: start; padding-block: 1rem; font-weight: 600; }
  th, td { padding: 0.85rem; text-align: start; border-block-end: 1px solid hsl(var(--line)); }
  :global(.article-guide .article-reading) { --article-reading-sticky-offset: 7rem; }
  :global(.article-guide .chapter-rail), :global(.article-guide .chapter-disclosure) { overflow-wrap: anywhere; }
  @media print { .article-guide { max-inline-size: none; } .article-guide__share { display: none; } table { min-inline-size: 0; } }
</style>
